# No scanner reads this file any more: the per-build Trivy gate was retired
# (constitution 1.40.0) and the fleet CVE check scans published images on a
# schedule (RT #1551). It is kept as the written record of accepted findings,
# which the Containerfile cites.
#
# This file is for findings nothing in this repo can fix. It is NOT the place
# to quiet a finding that an upgrade would clear: as of 2026-11-08 the
# Containerfile pins pillow, aiohttp, yarl, PyJWT and certifi above upstream's
# uv.lock, and bumps the base image's pip, precisely so those findings do not
# have to live here. Scott's ruling that day was "upgrade it as necessary" --
# so if a new finding has a fixed version, bump the pin and leave this file
# alone. Read the divergence block in the Containerfile before adding an entry.
#
# Three PyJWT HIGHs, one PyJWT CRITICAL, two more PyJWT HIGHs and one msgpack
# HIGH were deleted from this file on 2026-11-08 because the PyJWT 2.14.0 pin
# and the pip 26.3 bump fix them outright. That is the shape every future
# entry should be measured against.

# setuptools, inside the base image's pip. Hummingbird's python:3.13 ships pip
# in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages, and Trivy files its vendored
# bundle under the aggregate "Python" target with no path and no "(METADATA)"
# marker, which is why these look like they come from nowhere.
#
# Not fixable by a pin: the version is frozen inside pip. The Containerfile
# upgrades pip to 26.3 (which does fix the vendored certifi and msgpack), but
# 26.3 still vendors setuptools 70.3.0, so these two survive the bump.
#
# Removing pip is unsafe because hermes-agent's tools/lazy_deps.py self-heals
# a lean install at runtime.
#
# Not reachable: both require pip to talk to a package index. This container
# never runs pip at runtime, has no direct egress (internal=true network), and
# reaches every tool through the Trentina gateway.
#
# Revisit when any of three things changes, whichever comes first: pip
# revendors setuptools above 70.3.0 (watch `src/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt` at the
# `PIP_VERSION` the Containerfile pins), Hummingbird's python:3.13 stops
# shipping pip so the bundle leaves the image, or this container gains direct
# egress or a reason to run pip at runtime -- which would end the
# unreachability argument on its own. Check at every `PIP_VERSION` bump.
#
#   HIGH    CVE-2025-47273  setuptools 70.3.0  path traversal in PackageIndex
#   MEDIUM  CVE-2026-59890  setuptools 83.0.0  MANIFEST.in exclusion bypass
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890

# anyio / httpcore2 / httpx2 — pinned by the `mcp` PyPI package's own extras
# metadata (mcp[...]'s dependency spec), not by hermes-agent or by anything
# in this Containerfile. Checked upstream's uv.lock at every tag from
# v2026.8.31 through v2026.9.24 (the one this image tracks): all still pin
# anyio==4.12.1, httpcore2==2.7.0, httpx2==2.7.0. No version of hermes-agent
# exists yet that resolves clean;
# this is blocked on the `mcp` package itself, upstream of upstream.
#
# Not reachable: same isolation as the entries above, more so per Scott
# (2026-09-20) — Kagetora sits behind Trentina and is not directly
# internet-reachable at all; an attacker would need the host or Trentina
# itself compromised first, at which point these three CVEs are moot.
#
#   CRITICAL  CVE-2026-63374  anyio 4.12.1       TLS cert spoofing via IDNA host encoding
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-84381  httpcore2 2.7.0    WebSocket traffic sent in plaintext via SOCKS5
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-84382  httpx2 2.7.0       DoS via streaming response decompression
CVE-2026-63374
CVE-2026-84381
CVE-2026-84382

# urllib3 2.7.0 -- upstream's uv.lock pins it at v2026.8.31, at v2026.9.24 and
# on main, and no upstream release has moved it. The PyJWT entries that used
# to sit in this block are gone: the Containerfile now pins PyJWT 2.14.0,
# which fixes all six of them plus GHSA-pxh4-856f-4h89.
#
# urllib3 is NOT pinned alongside it, deliberately. These two are accepted
# findings, not blocking ones, and the 2026-11-08 divergence was kept to the
# packages that were actually failing the gate. Pinning urllib3>=2.8.0 is the
# obvious next candidate and wants its own review.
#
# Accepted by Scott (2026-10-01): no direct egress, every outbound call
# through the Trentina gateway. Whether any path uses an HTTPS proxy through
# urllib3 was not traced -- this is an acceptance of unchanged exposure, not a
# finding that the code is unreachable. Remove when upstream's lockfile moves
# to urllib3>=2.8.0, or when a pin lands in the Containerfile.
#
#   HIGH  CVE-2026-97687  urllib3 2.7.0  traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS config override
#   HIGH  CVE-2026-97689  urllib3 2.7.0  DoS via unbounded allocation in chunk parser
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
